// Scope of the three aids (CCH Livre VIII, Titres III-IV): APL dwelling and
// occupant cases, post-2017 loan exclusions, the six ALF household categories,
// the residual ALS, accession-allocation debts, the pregnancy assimilation and
// the family-benefits bridge.
//
// INPUT CONTRACT (case facts, all origin case_input unless noted):
// agency-established classifications at the article's own level: cas_apl_l831_1
// (the 6 dwelling cases), occupant_apl_r831_1 (the 4 occupant cases),
// dette_accession_allocation (the 3 R. 842-5 debts), loan signature dates,
// the four family-benefit receipt flags (explicit booleans; false means the
// agency established non-receipt), and household-composition findings
// (enfant_charge_l512_3, menage_nouveaux_maries, ascendant_charge_age_determine,
// proche_handicape_charge, femme_seule_enceinte). Raw dwelling facts (aid and
// loan characteristics, convention texts, the R. 321-15 work list, the
// D. 331-63 technical norms, the L. 831-2 commune list) are NOT inputs: the
// agency establishes the article-level category and the case carries it.
// Eligibility heads (eligible_apl/alf/als) are ADVISORY: they do not gate
// droit_ouvert or any calculation module, which keep reading aide_demandee and
// their own facts. Wiring eligibility as a gate is an owner follow-up (it
// would change existing derivations); the priority and exclusion logic below
// is fully executable on its own heads.
//
// DEONTIC MAP (this module is entitlement classification, no duties):
// L. 831-1/R. 831-1 grant APL by case conjunction; L. 831-2 excludes
// post-2017 loans (defeater) with the 2018-2019 double-condition exception
// (lex-specialis restorer); L. 841-4 excludes unconditionally (defeaters);
// L. 841-1 grants ALF by household category; L. 841-2 grants ALS residually
// (defeasible, defeated by attributed APL/ALF); L. 841-3 extends ALS to
// long-stay residents; R. 842-5 classifies accession debts; R. 841-2 deems
// the lone pregnant woman childless for the calculation; L. 821-3 publishes
// the family-benefits exclusion marker, household and child level (effect
// in pf-core).
// L. 841-5 (ALS non-cumul and difference) lives in 11-exclusivite with the
// attribution layer it qualifies.
//
// OPEN-WORLD CAVEAT (recorded, not hidden): the residual ALS defeats on
// ATTRIBUTED apl/alf (scope joined with the request: the package's
// institutional notion of "beneficier", L. 841-2). Bare eligibility without
// attribution no longer excludes. Payment-level receipt is aid-untyped in
// the core (aide_versee/aide_mensuelle carry no aid), so attribution-level
// benefit is the adopted reading; the versement nuance is a boundary.
// A case that supplies no scope inputs derives no attribution, so ALS
// defaults eligible when requested; unassessed scope is not ineligibility.
//
// FRAGMENTS (predicted; reviewer verifies after sync --write): base + all 7
// _ED fragments for each cited article (all stable since 2019-09-01).

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package fr.apl version "0.1.0";
namespace "urn:fr:corpus:clir:apl";

